{#- Services (REQ-010 as amended by A-02; plan D-14): three article.card.service
    blocks on the balanced subgrid — number | title | text | "What you get"
    heading | list (2–4 items) | action — the six tracks base.css spans.
    Headings, texts and lists come from strings.themes.<key> (the keys stay
    ai-apps / ai-adoption / investing so the apps data keeps validating); the
    app-development card acts through the primary mailto:, the other two
    through #apps anchors. The copy bands (title ≤ 20 characters, texts within
    a 25 % band) are asserted by tests/apps.test.mjs. -#}
{%- set services = strings[lang].services -%}
<section id="services" class="section" aria-labelledby="services-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ services.eyebrow }}</p>
      <h2 id="services-title">{{ services.heading }}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="service-grid">
      {%- for key in ["ai-apps", "ai-adoption", "investing"] %}
      {%- set theme = strings[lang].themes[key] %}
      <article class="card service reveal">
        <p class="num">0{{ loop.index }}</p>
        <h3>{{ theme.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ theme.text }}</p>
        <h4 class="gets-heading">{{ theme.getsHeading }}</h4>
        <ul class="gets">
          {%- for itemKey, item in theme.gets %}
          <li>{{ item }}</li>
          {%- endfor %}
        </ul>
        <a class="text-link" href="{{ strings[lang].hero.ctaPrimary | mailtoSubject if key == "ai-apps" else "#apps" }}">{{ theme.cta }}<span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </article>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
